{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-volume-form-formula","title":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form-formula","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1607,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:hypersurface-volume-form-formula","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:interior-multiplication]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:volume-form-pointwise]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-uniqueness]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-value-one]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form-formula","line":2701,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Equation (2.17)]\n\\label{prop:hypersurface-volume-form-formula}\n\n\\uses{def:interior-multiplication, def:unit-normal, lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal, lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis, def:volume-form-pointwise, prop:volume-form-uniqueness, prop:volume-form-value-one, def:metric-preserving}\n\n\n\n\nLet $F:M\\to\\widetilde M$ be an isometric immersion of an $n$-manifold into an oriented Riemannian $(n+1)$-manifold. If $N_x$ is unit normal and a local oriented orthonormal frame $(E_i)$ has adapted basis $(N_x,dF_xE_i)$ positively oriented, then\n\\begin{equation}\ndV_g|_x=\\bigl((N\\lrcorner dV_{\\widetilde g})|_M\\bigr)_x. \\tag{2.17}\n\\end{equation}\nHere the right side maps $(v_1,\\ldots,v_n)$ to $dV_{\\widetilde g}|_{F(x)}(N_x,dF_xv_1,\\ldots,dF_xv_n)$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:interior-multiplication,lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal,lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis,prop:volume-form-uniqueness,prop:volume-form-value-one}\n\\sketch On $(E_i)$, the contracted ambient form evaluates to $1$ because the adapted family is a positively oriented orthonormal ambient basis. Proposition \\ref{prop:volume-form-uniqueness} identifies it with $dV_g|_x$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Equation (2.17)] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a6879706572737572666163652d766f6c756d652d666f726d2d666f726d756c61\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ainterior-multiplication\">↗ def:interior-multiplication</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aunit-normal\">↗ def:unit-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aadapted-frame-cons-normal\">↗ lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aadapted-frame-ambient-basis\">↗ lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Avolume-form-pointwise\">↗ def:volume-form-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-uniqueness\">↗ prop:volume-form-uniqueness</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-value-one\">↗ prop:volume-form-value-one</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ametric-preserving\">↗ def:metric-preserving</a> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F:M\\to \\widetilde M$\">$F:M\\to \\widetilde M$</span> be an isometric immersion of an <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-manifold into an oriented Riemannian <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(n+1)$\">$(n+1)$</span>-manifold. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N_x$\">$N_x$</span> is unit normal and a local oriented orthonormal frame <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(E_i)$\">$(E_i)$</span> has adapted basis <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(N_x,dF_xE_i)$\">$(N_x,dF_xE_i)$</span> positively oriented, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\begin{equation}  dV_g|_x=\\bigl((N\\lrcorner dV_{\\widetilde g})|_M\\bigr)_x. \\tag {2.17} \\end{equation}\">\\begin{equation}  dV_g|_x=\\bigl((N\\lrcorner dV_{\\widetilde g})|_M\\bigr)_x. \\tag {2.17} \\end{equation}</span> Here the right side maps <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(v_1,\\ldots ,v_n)$\">$(v_1,\\ldots ,v_n)$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dV_{\\widetilde g}|_{F(x)}(N_x,dF_xv_1,\\ldots ,dF_xv_n)$\">$dV_{\\widetilde g}|_{F(x)}(N_x,dF_xv_1,\\ldots ,dF_xv_n)$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ainterior-multiplication\">↗ def:interior-multiplication</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aadapted-frame-cons-normal\">↗ lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aadapted-frame-ambient-basis\">↗ lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-uniqueness\">↗ prop:volume-form-uniqueness</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-value-one\">↗ prop:volume-form-value-one</a> \\sketch On <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(E_i)$\">$(E_i)$</span>, the contracted ambient form evaluates to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span> because the adapted family is a positively oriented orthonormal ambient basis. Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Avolume-form-uniqueness\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-uniqueness\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a766f6c756d652d666f726d2d756e697175656e657373\">12</a> identifies it with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dV_g|_x$\">$dV_g|_x$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:nonvanishing-top-form-orientation","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:interior-multiplication","title":"def:interior-multiplication","label":"def:interior-multiplication"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal","title":"def:unit-normal","label":"def:unit-normal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal","title":"lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal","label":"lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis","title":"lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis","label":"lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:volume-form-pointwise","title":"def:volume-form-pointwise","label":"def:volume-form-pointwise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-uniqueness","title":"prop:volume-form-uniqueness","label":"prop:volume-form-uniqueness"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-value-one","title":"prop:volume-form-value-one","label":"prop:volume-form-value-one"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving","title":"def:metric-preserving","label":"def:metric-preserving"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-volume-form","title":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form","label":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prob:hypersurface-volume-form","title":"prob:hypersurface-volume-form","label":"prob:hypersurface-volume-form"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-volume-form-formula","title":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form-formula","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[Equation (2.17)]\n\\label{prop:hypersurface-volume-form-formula}\n\n\\uses{def:interior-multiplication, def:unit-normal, lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal, lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis, def:volume-form-pointwise, prop:volume-form-uniqueness, prop:volume-form-value-one, def:metric-preserving}\n\n\n\n\nLet $F:M\\to\\widetilde M$ be an isometric immersion of an $n$-manifold into an oriented Riemannian $(n+1)$-manifold. If $N_x$ is unit normal and a local oriented orthonormal frame $(E_i)$ has adapted basis $(N_x,dF_xE_i)$ positively oriented, then\n\\begin{equation}\ndV_g|_x=\\bigl((N\\lrcorner dV_{\\widetilde g})|_M\\bigr)_x. \\tag{2.17}\n\\end{equation}\nHere the right side maps $(v_1,\\ldots,v_n)$ to $dV_{\\widetilde g}|_{F(x)}(N_x,dF_xv_1,\\ldots,dF_xv_n)$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:interior-multiplication,lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal,lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis,prop:volume-form-uniqueness,prop:volume-form-value-one}\n\\sketch On $(E_i)$, the contracted ambient form evaluates to $1$ because the adapted family is a positively oriented orthonormal ambient basis. Proposition \\ref{prop:volume-form-uniqueness} identifies it with $dV_g|_x$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:interior-multiplication","title":"def:interior-multiplication","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal","title":"def:unit-normal","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal","title":"lem:adapted-frame-cons-normal","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis","title":"lem:adapted-frame-ambient-basis","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:volume-form-pointwise","title":"def:volume-form-pointwise","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-uniqueness","title":"prop:volume-form-uniqueness","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-value-one","title":"prop:volume-form-value-one","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving","title":"def:metric-preserving","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}